<!--
  Agent-Stamp: 00000000-muse-7e57-d0c5-58316a922026

  Entitlements for the Mac App Store bundle, prepared
  2026-11-21 with runner/tools/apple_store.py and extended
  2026-11-23. The store requires the App Sandbox on every
  Mac App Store app. Two further entries stand here, each
  answering a named finding, and no further entitlement
  joins this file quietly; each one is a claim the review
  reads.

  com.apple.security.network.client: the runner initiates
  its mailbox and HTTPS connections, and under the App
  Sandbox those outgoing connections are refused without
  this entitlement (outside review, 2026-11-23).

  com.apple.application-identifier: the first upload came
  back with TestFlight warning 90886, the bundle lacked an
  application identifier in its signature. The value joins
  the team ID and the bundle ID and matches the embedded
  provisioning profile (Homing Pigeon Mac App Store).

  The sandbox still cannot hold what the runner does on a
  customer's machine, which is the known shape of this
  submission: the owner directed that it be attempted
  anyway and App Review be allowed to give the answer (the
  record stands in docs/steady/design/auto-publish-design.md).
  runner/tools/apple_store.py pins this file's parsed form
  as EXPECTED_ENTITLEMENTS and refuses to plan an upload
  when the file drifts from it.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
	<string>3PH9A88USW.ai.pigeon-home.homing-pigeon</string>
</dict>
</plist>
